I have not previously seen the issue you described in your post. I ran the function on a few datasets I have handy to check, and it worked without error. Thus it is not obvious whether this issue is data specific (and thus requires something on your end), or whether there is an error in the code that other datasets are not triggering.

To diagnose the problem further I would need you to send me your data and code off-line. Then I’ll try to carve out some time to investigate.

Best,

